WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.510
There are three ropes in front of you.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.730
Choose one and pull it.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.550
That water will soon spread 
to all the support beams.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.620
They will become unable to bear the weight
and will collapse.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.340
If you wish to save yourself,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.280
you must first pull the rope 
to close the water gate.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.060
However...

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.950
If you pull either of the wrong ropes,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.040
the ruins will completely collapse.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.130
Huh? What the heck is that?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.600
They'll completely collapse?

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.460
I don't get it!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>Which one?</i>

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.300
<i>Which is attached, and how?</i>

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.650
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.540
<i>It's too complex; I can't get it!</i>

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.770
<i>If I don't hurry, Nonoha will...</i>

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.690
Kaito!

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.690
Dammit!

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.610
Kaito?

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.540
Kaito, what's the matter?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.410
Are you okay?

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:24.100
Shut up.
Are you okay?

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.440
Kaito...

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.610
This one's a dummy.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.900
This one, too.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.360
And this one.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.490
Kaito, the door opened!

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.980
Kaito?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.030
Kaito! Hold on!

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.680
Kaito! Kaito!

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.070
Better than I expected, Kaito Daimon.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.990
We're saved, Kaito.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.910
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.640
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.490
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.230
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.740
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.450
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.670
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.320
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.330
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.630
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.390
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:22.890
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.190
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.880
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.100
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.440
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.070
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:42.960
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.640
Brain diver

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.440
Brain diver

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:02.010
The Philosopher's Reward

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.650
Come on!

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.610
How long you gonna sleep, Kaito?

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:18.460
I finished up my morning 
practice to come here.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.490
<i>What was that, I wonder?</i>

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.990
<i>He's not still like that, right?</i>

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.440
Whoa, what's with this 
puzzle? It's so difficult!

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.440
There's no way even Kaito could solve it!

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.500
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:37.920
Huh?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.670
<i>Good, he's the same Kaito as always.</i>

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.950
Hurry and get up!

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.920
Sleepyhead! Lazybones! Bed louse!

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.090
Okay...

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.140
Then the armlet sparkled, and...

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.600
Hey, are you listening?

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.580
What was that?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.210
It felt like I'd become 
one with the puzzle.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.270
Was that...

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.320
because of this armlet?

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.300
Good morning.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.200
Good morning.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.080
Not loud enough!

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:16.400
G..Good morning!

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.440
Good morning, Miss Vice President.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:19.900
Good morning.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.750
Good morning!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.360
Hey! Kaito Daimo-

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.130
Kaito Daimon!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:27.760
Me?

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.540
Moron!

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.310
Ron, mo, ron, ron, ron!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.020
Ron, ron, ron, mo!

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.320
Mo, moron, moron!

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.320
Ron, ron! Mo, mo!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.270
Ron, ron, mo!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.270
Who the heck is that?

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.610
So you are a moron after all.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.750
I always thought, "What a moron,"
and I guess you are.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.700
You're wrong!

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.480
Kaito Daimon!

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.830
Ron, mo, ron, ron, ron!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.740
What is this?

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.450
Sounds like some Buddhist chant
from the south, huh?

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.310
No, it's a new kind of rap.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.170
It's Morse Code.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.020
"Mo" is a long tone, and "ron" is short.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.040
He's screwin' with me!

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.060
Kaito!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.720
"I'll wait on the roof," he says?!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:23.230
Use the 4 pieces
to make a "T"!!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.430
"Use the four pieces to make a T?"

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:27.590
Piece of cake.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.590
Wait, Kaito!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.060
The puzzle, it's solved...

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.920
Connect the 9 dots using
4 continuous lines!!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.920
"Connect the nine dots using 
four continuous lines"?

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.300
Simple!

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:50.130
What numbers go in A and B?!

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:48.410
"What numbers go in A and B?!"

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.130
That's way too easy!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.220
Oh, sure enough, they're connected
with four continuous lines.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.940
Why these numbers?

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.400
Who's up here going, 
"Moron, moron, moron"?!

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:11.230
Morons have no business 
with Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.840
So you're the one-

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:16.380
Anyone who interferes with my
profits will pay the price!

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:18.100
Who are you, bastard?!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.580
My name is Gammon Sakanoue!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.790
I hold the title of Galileo.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.830
The title of Galileo?

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.420
Got it, moron?!

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.930
Bastard! Wait up, dammit!

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.710
Ugh, I used my brain more 
than I should have...

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.260
That son of a bitch, next time I see him,

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.260
What are you doing, Kaito?

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.140
he'll be the one that will pay the price!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.540
Now, now, don't be so angry.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:44.810
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.320
The principal is calling 
for you, Mr. Kaito Daimon.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.740
That armlet...

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:56.730
It suits you.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.120
What can I do for ya?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:03.120
That was excellent work solving the
puzzle of the ruins, Kaito Daimon.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.630
How do you know about that?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.190
Because that, the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:12.600
was the prize sealed within the ruins.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.280
Armlet of Orpheus?

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:18.390
You released the prize 
and entered into a pact.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:23.160
The Armlet of Orpheus is 
proof of the chosen Solver.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.130
It is a legendary prize, said to

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:28.480
awaken the
sleeping potential within its pact holder.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.010
I'm extremely interested in what sort

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.190
of abilities it has awakened in you.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:40.300
I suppose offering you 
a scholarship to our

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.000
Gakuen was not in vain.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.130
I don't understand!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.930
I don't care, and I 
don't need this thing,

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.870
so hurry up and get it offa me!

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.070
That's impossible.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.050
You're the pact holder, Kaito.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.800
When the armlet was made, and by whom,

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.840
is completely unknown.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:00.810
What is known is that, going forward,
you will be a Solver

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:04.310
and you will fight the Givers of the POG.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.850
Rather, I would ask that you do so.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.030
And what's the POG?

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.890
They are a think tank,
 those who make and

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.560
oversee the Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.280
That is the POG.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.200
What do you mean, "fight" them?

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.950
Explain yourself!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.280
Come on, calm-

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.160
What's all this about prizes and
Philosopher's Puzzles?!

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.160
You know the pyramids, right?

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.170
Huh?

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.080
Would you believe it if I said that

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.260
they're puzzles created long ago?

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.240
Since ancient times, 
many of those in power

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.390
have sealed their riches inside barriers

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:39.390
called Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.380
And those Philosopher's Puzzles were

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:45.160
made by the POG think tank.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.810
Philosopher's Puzzles...

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.930
They are nothing more than battlegrounds

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:52.690
for the POG's Givers and
the Solvers who solve puzzles.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.840
But why Kaito?

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.820
Yeah! This has got nothin' to do with me.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:02.580
The ultimate goal of the POG is...

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.080
to release the Puzzle of God.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:06.520
Huh?

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.000
Those who survive the fight,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.800
those who possess the ultimate intellect:

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:15.050
only they may challenge 
the Puzzle of God.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:18.390
When it is solved,
man may stand on the same level as God.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.090
So it is said.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.390
The Puzzle of God?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.600
Correct.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.150
However, this comes with a price.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.660
Going forward, a portion 
of prizes you receive

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.760
will be split between you and the Gakuen.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.570
Once again, Kaito Daimon:

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.430
as a Solver with the title 
of Einstein, will you-

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:38.010
Mo, mo, mo, mo.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.320
Ron, ron, moron, ron.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.570
Moron, mo, moron, mo, moron.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.950
So, you refuse?

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.370
I don't understand this "title" stuff,
and I don't need it.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.370
Also...

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.380
I like puzzles, but I ain't 
gonna let you guys use me!

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.020
You're still mad, Kaito?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.260
Course I am!

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.350
And I'm super pissed 
at being made to solve

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.470
that weirdo's puzzles this morning!

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.190
It's times like this that you should eat!

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.050
When you're solving puzzles,
your brain consumes a lot of energy.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:19.520
Solving one puzzle could make you lose
as much as three kilograms!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.760
Hey, Pops!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.020
Double fried fish special,
a ton of shredded cabbage,

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.590
udon noodles and some curry.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:27.750
Bastard!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.430
Got a good appetite today too, huh?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.040
Goin' up against an moron...

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.040
makes a body hungry!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.210
I can't take it anymore!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.210
Okay, okay, no fighting.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.760
Wow, a perfect Full Nelson!

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.890
That's upperclassman Nonoha for you!

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.180
Let me go!

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.300
You Galileo sonovabitch!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.300
I won't rest till I kick your ass!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.310
"Galileo" is upperclassman 
Gammon's title, isn't it?

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.310
You know him?

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.360
Yes! He's been scouted by the
Puzzle Club before,

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.310
but he didn't join.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.690
Kaito!

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.530
Double fried fish special,
a megaton of shredded cabbage,

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.990
udon noodles, curry and a tempura bowl!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:08.330
Bein' made to solve dumb-ass puzzles
makes a body hungry.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:10.690
Pops!

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.870
Add a tempura bowl and some
juicy fried chicken bites!

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.570
I add juicy fried chicken bites
and sweet-and-sour pork!

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:19.010
And your special rice 
omelette with the works!

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:22.220
Add a sweet-and-sour pork,
your special rice omelette with the works,

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.990
and hearty-licious tsukemen 
noodles with extra leeks!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.850
I add hearty-licious tsukemen noodles
with a ton of leeks!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.350
Kaito, I thought you hated leeks.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.730
I can eat 'em! I can totally eat 'em!

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:32.680
Really?

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:35.030
Also, a strawberry parfait for dessert.
Really?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.190
I..I'll have a strawberry parfait, too.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.280
And five daifuku rice cakes!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:44.320
That'll be 3,250 yen.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.610
Huh? Hey, he didn't pay!

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.580
Gammon has a title, so his is free.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.440
It's free if you have a title?!

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:53.200
That's right.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.380
Okay, 3,250 yen.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.330
Dammit!

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:01.380
An excellent meal.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:08.290
A 3,000-yen lunch for free, and...

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.700
Next up is the leeks, huh?

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:11.890
You're an idiot, aren't you?

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.490
Still, these "titles" are great, huh?

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:18.650
Yes, well, they give you special privileges
throughout the school!

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.860
I'd like to have a title someday, too!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.780
After royalty, like 
Himiko or Ono no Imoko!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.660
<i>I am Clash, a Giver of the POG.</i>

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:35.060
<i>We have received a request 
to release a prize.</i>

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:39.380
<i>I appoint you, Kaito Daimon,
the Solver of this Philosopher's Puzzle.</i>

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.300
So, this means, "Come here"?

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.340
I guess so.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.380
Snatch!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.300
Hey!
Snatch!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.300
You won't be needin' this.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.910
A Philosopher's Puzzle...

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.210
Finally, I've found one.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.390
I'll profit nicely from this!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.270
All he does is talk about 
profit, the stingy bastard.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.600
You can only do puzzles 
for money, or what?

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.960
You stupid kid!

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.920
My brain cells make money.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.690
Is any other reason necessary?

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.370
In any case, don't be gettin' in my way.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.290
I hate that guy!

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:15.080
Still, an invitation to solve 
a Philosopher's Puzzle...

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.330
I just hope he doesn't 
run into any danger.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.820
The placement of the numbers...
The balance...

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.300
All of it coming at me at once.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.350
It's as if I'm being tested.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:33.510
I don't care for this, 
but it's a good puzzle.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.280
<i>That's a good puzzle, 
Kaito, and just like you.</i>

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.190
<i>Really?</i>

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:46.820
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:51.090
<i>Looking at a puzzle tells you
about the person who made it.</i>

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.830
<i>Encountering a puzzle means
encountering a person.</i>

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:59.540
<i>That, too, is a single piece 
of the puzzle called "fate."</i>

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:08.220
That bastard Galileo is trying
to make a good puzzle, and I...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.270
You going?

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:15.720
You can't leave some dangerous
puzzle alone, can you?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.470
Nonoha...

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.480
I looked at the map, so I've got the
location good and memorized.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.230
Your memory, if nothing 
else, really is awesome.

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.610
You can leave off "if nothing else"!

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.240
Puzzle time, let's begin!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.280
You've got five hours, 
then I'm going home!

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.630
I've been waiting for you, Kaito Daimon.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.340
I am Clash, a POG Giver.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.050
Welcome to my Philosopher's Puzzle!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.680
If you are prepared to 
challenge this puzzle...

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.020
then get in the red car!

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.010
So this is a Philosopher's Puzzle?

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.190
A full-scale parking lot puzzle...

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:05.320
Who are you?

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.090
The one who solves that puzzle

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.780
shall be the genius at the 
center of all puzzles...

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:13.490
Galileo, aka Gammon Sakanoue!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.060
I cannot allow someone not appointed
to attempt the challenge.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.280
You scared?

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:21.750
Worried I might solve your puzzle?

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:22.790
What?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.970
You fool!

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.450
Only those with the greatest of intellect

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.050
may challenge this puzzle!

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:31.730
Then it's perfect for me.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.430
Get off your high horse already!

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.760
I'll be the one to solve that puzzle!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.270
Bastard! Kaito Daimon!

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:40.540
I thought I told you:

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:43.270
interfere with my profits 
and you'll pay the price!

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.870
I was the one appointed for this.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:46.330
Step back!

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:47.690
Quit tryin' to butt in.
Step back!

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.530
Huh?! You're the one who butted in first!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:54.480
All three of you, get into 
the red car together!

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.360
That one, right?

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:03.050
Whoa! There's no steering wheel!

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.240
Moron! It's on the left-hand side.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.300
Okay, okay, okay, okay!

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.990
It is not the steering 
wheel that controls it.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:10.630
What?!
It is not the steering wheel that controls it.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.130
Do so using this touch panel!

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:14.930
You use the steering wheel, sucker!

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:15.510
Shut up!
You use the steering wheel, sucker!

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.260
The Giver and the Solvers 
have assembled...

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:23.350
And now, the battle of wits
to release the prize shall begin!

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.230
We're locked in!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.740
The one who desired this barrier to

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.350
be released was Baron Kaidou!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.380
The prize is that red car.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.700
Get it out in one piece 
and victory is yours.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.830
Baron Kaidou is the 
school principal, right?

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:40.800
That guy's gotten involved again?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.700
<i>However, if you fail...</i>

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:48.480
<i>That motor coach shall 
fall atop your heads!</i>

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.590
No way!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.450
If he does that, this whole car will...

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.590
Another deadly puzzle, huh?

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:57.260
Moron! This car's an antique.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.720
He wouldn't do that; it's a bluff.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.800
Bastard, when did you...

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.990
This looks like it will 
turn a nice profit!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.600
You really piss me off.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.690
Your time limit is ten minutes.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.100
And now, begin!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.090
I don't need no ten minutes.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:12.980
Let's go.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.760
This will be a cinch.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:37.380
Th..That's...

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.640
Last move.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.750
Incredible.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.720
Well, well, we still 
got two minutes left.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.180
What a shame.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.230
Shall I make the last move?!

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.280
Shut up! Just do it already!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:58.200
To think, there was a Solver of such
skill other than Kaito Daimon...

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.280
It can't be helped.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.280
Okay, here goes.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.250
What happened?

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.290
It stopped?!

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.840
<i>That car has been immobilized.</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:11.790
What?!

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:15.660
My apologies, it is simply an accident.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.900
You all shall die here.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.300
Unfortunately.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:23.800
However, the fact that my puzzle
wins remains unchanged.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.980
For real? You're gonna crush the prize?!

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:28.560
<i>I care not!</i>

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.100
No way!

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:31.600
<i>I cannot allow my puzzle</i>

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.150
to be solved by scum like you!

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.400
Dammit!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.780
I ain't goin' out! Not like this!

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:40.610
I'm gonna use these brains
for more and more profit!

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.940
That son of a bitch!

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.870
But this puzzle...

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.210
This puzzle wants to be solved!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.130
Be crushed!

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.950
E quebra-cabeça
And the puzzles

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.770
Eu quero ver quem vai fazer
I want to see who will do them

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:01.840
Oh, no!

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:04.560
O quebra-cabeça
The puzzles

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.760
Dammit! Help out, you bastard!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.040
We gotta get out!

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:08.750
E quebra-cabeça
And the puzzles

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:08.650
The puzzle...

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:10.940
This thing is saying, "Solve me!"

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.920
Eu quero ver quem vai vencer
I want to see who will be solver

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:12.810
Do quebra-cabeça
Of the puzzles

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:13.310
Dumbass! There's no way we can solve it!

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:17.710
Eu quero ver quem vai ganhar
I want to see who will be the winner

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.620
Eu quero ver quem vai perder
I want to see who will be the loser

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:24.320
Do quebra, quebra, pra valer
Of the puzzles, the puzzles, for real

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.200
What's that? What's goin' on?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.320
Kaito, again?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.410
Solved it.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.740
Bastard, quit yer bluffin'!

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:30.830
Shut up.

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:36.810
It can't be!

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:44.050
What?!

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:00.770
Something like this...

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.360
Kaito...

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:06.280
Kaito!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.830
It's the same as last time.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.200
That's a first for me.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:14.680
Such a big, dumb bastard...

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.420
If he weren't, he never woulda
thought of a solution like that.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.010
I give you the prize.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:22.580
Fixin' it looks like it will cost a lot.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:25.870
I don't need it.

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.740
Kaito, you're awake?

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:32.210
This armlet saved us again, huh?

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:34.940
Wrong! It was my skill!

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:39.330
In any case, I'll accept 
this title of "Einstein."

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:40.840
Oh, really?

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.230
After all, I'm hungry.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.690
Oh, so that's why.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:47.170
Yes, that ability is indeed yours,

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.820
a skill drawn out from you 
by the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:53.660
You are a wonderful specimen.

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:58.840
The Phi-Brain children, eh?

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:03.490
<i>My Giver status, revoked?!</i>

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:07.660
It has been determined that you
are not befitting the POG.

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:10.470
A puzzle with no solution lacks beauty.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:12.260
<i>Please wait! Let me-</i>

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:19.060
The pact holder of Orpheus seems to

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:22.100
have considerable latent abilities.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:23.440
His name is...

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:25.620
Kaito Daimon.

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:41.560
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:47.480
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:52.110
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:57.160
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:02.640
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:08.000
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:13.180
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:18.430
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:23.770
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:26.450
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:29.360
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:33.930
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:39.230
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:44.510
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.510 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.990
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:06.050
Puzzles aren't meant for geniuses to do.

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:09.520
A genius must use his 
mind to help others.

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:10.630
Who the heck are you?

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:12.480
You're suddenly criticizing our show?

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:14.720
Better watch what you say,
or you won't be appearing!

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:16.340
Not to worry:

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:18.930
the position of uppity young boy is

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:21.600
absolutely essential for this program.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:24.290
Next time: "The Melancholy 
of a Boy Genius"

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:27.210
The Melancholy of a Boy Genius

00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:27.190
This guy's calculated his own character!
